is this art or is it racism an  exhibition that's been shown in 12 other  cities around the world has been shut  down in London before it even began on  its opening night protesters surrounded  exhibit b an installation by a white  South African artist it features black  actors shackled and chained in cages and  claims to explore the legacy of slavery  and racial oppression but only a handful  of people were able to see it with  protesters forcing the doors closed  because of the protest and for the  protestors there's a real sense of  victory the Barbican says it could not  guarantee the safety of those involved  but speaking to Sky News beforehand it  defended the show people feel that this  show is somehow racist it isn't it is a  very important exploration of issues  surrounding racism it draws on the human  zoos of previous centuries freak shows  in which people seen as abnormal were  displayed black people amongst them one  with Sarah Baartman  a slave known as Hottentot Venus who  entertained European audiences in the  1800s this dancer who took part in  Exhibit B in Paris says she tried to put  on something similar herself but found  little interest in her perspective where  white people can do it they can choose  to do it and and the program matters  take them take the project because they  say they are more  distant to do it and the black people  they never take the project because we  don't have enough distance to do it and  I can understand the black people will  be fed up with this Exhibit B has now  been cancelled but the Rao over where  freedom of expression ends and racism  begins continues fo Hirsch Stein news
 

